  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Lead Gen Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a lead generation landing page?\", \"a\": \"A lead generation landing page is a standalone page with one job: getting visitors to submit their contact details in exchange for an offer such as a demo or a free trial. Marketers also call it a lead capture landing page.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build a lead gen landing page?\", \"a\": \"Settle the offer and the person who follows up before you design anything. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe both in one prompt and get the page with its form and lead table. Changes are made by sending another message.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the biggest mistake on lead gen landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Collecting leads that nobody answers. A lead gen landing page can work perfectly while its submissions pile up in an inbox no one owns. Name the person who calls back before launch, route each lead to them, and send visitors to a thank you page that says when to expect that call.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good cost per lead for a lead capture landing page?\", \"a\": \"Any figure below the value of a lead to you. Multiply what a new customer brings in by the share of leads that become customers. If a customer brings $2,000 and one lead in 20 buys, any cost per lead under $100 pays for itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you build an email capture landing page for free?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a page with its form. A single-field email capture landing page, such as a squeeze page, is a good first build on a free plan.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a lead gen landing page include?\", \"a\": \"One offer and the few parts that sell it. Good landing page design for lead generation is plain: a headline that repeats the ad, a short paragraph on what the visitor gets, and proof beside the form. Nothing on the page links anywhere else.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best landing pages for lead generation?\", \"a\": \"The best landing pages for lead generation make one offer and ask only for what the follow-up needs. A software demo page might want a work address and headcount, while a gym pass needs a name and a phone number. Each one tells the visitor what happens after they submit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How much does it cost to create a lead gen landing page?\", \"a\": \"The cost depends on who builds it. A designer charges a project fee, and builders price their monthly plans by visitor count or by list size. Emergent generates the page from a prompt on its free tier, a custom domain uses credits, and ad spend is a separate line.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which fields should a lead capture landing page collect?\", \"a\": \"Only the ones the follow-up will use. A guide needs nothing more than an email address, while a demo request may add company size to decide which rep calls back. With Emergent, each submission lands in a database you own, not in a vendor dashboard.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find lead generation landing page templates?\", \"a\": \"Builder galleries are the usual place to start with lead generation landing page templates. Your own market is often more useful: note what competitors ask for in their forms, then pair your page with a lead capture form built around your own fields.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}